Say which state the game is in.

A port is debugged from a log and a screen, and the screen only shows what a state managed
to draw - so a transition that happened and rendered nothing looks exactly like one that
never happened. That cost an evening: pressing Play appeared to restart the menu, and
whether it had reached the name screen, reached the level select and bounced, or never
fired at all could not be told apart from outside the machine.

With this line it took one run. The log read

    state: st_title -> st_name     the name screen was reached
    state: st_name  -> st_set      the name was accepted
    state: st_set   -> st_title    and the level select bounced straight off

which is a different problem from the one it looked like. Two more lines - the button
dispatch and the menu token - narrowed it to one keypress arriving as two activations, and
came out again once it had; this one stays, because knowing where the game is is not a
question that gets answered once.

The addresses resolve against `build/neverball.map`, where every `st_*` is a symbol.

diff --git a/share/state.c b/share/state.c
index d0c2dcd..697fb4b 100644
--- a/share/state.c
+++ b/share/state.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include "config.h"
 #include "video.h"
 #include "common.h"
+#include "log.h"
 #include "hmd.h"
 #include "geom.h"
 
@@ -125,6 +126,15 @@ int goto_state(struct state *st)
 {
     struct state *prev = state;
 
+    /* **Every state change, named by address.** A port is debugged from a log and a screen, and
+     * the screen only shows what a state managed to draw - so a transition that happens and
+     * renders nothing looks exactly like one that never happened. That cost most of an evening:
+     * pressing Play appeared to restart the menu, and whether it had reached the name screen or
+     * bounced off it could not be told apart from the outside. The addresses resolve against
+     * build/neverball.map, where every `st_*` is a symbol. */
+    log_printf("state: %p -> %p (enter=%p)\n",
+               (void *) prev, (void *) st, st ? (void *) st->enter : NULL);
+
     if (state && state->leave)
         state->leave(state, st, state->gui_id);
 
